@ 37.1.2.4 - Proto-Northern Iroquoian to Proto-Mohawk-Oneida
# citation: cedh audmanh, from Julian, Charles (2010), “A History of the Iroquoian Languages”,
# 			University of Manitoba, Winnipeg
	ẽ(ː) õ(ː) > ʌ̃(ː) ũ(ː)
	t͡s > hs / V_{t,k(ʷ)}
	t͡s > s // _{h,i,j}
	ns > t͡s / _{t,k(ʷ)}
	n > ∅ / _s
	”V > ”V:[+ long, +falling tone] / _{ʔ,hR}
	ʔ > ∅ / ”V:[+ long, +falling tone]_C
	h > ∅ / ”V:[+ long, +falling tone]_R
	h > ∅ / _#
	h > ∅ / #_w
	V:[+ long] > V / _(C)(C)(C)#
	CʔV₀ > CV₀ʔV₀
	∅ > e / w_r (and “probably. . .in other environments”)